  "content": {
    "id": "p28-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Expand each series for a few terms. Then write down $a$ and $r$, and find the limiting sum.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p28-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^n$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac15+\\frac1{25}+\\frac1{125}+\\cdots$; $a=\\frac15$, $r=\\frac15$; $S_\\infty=\\frac14$.",
          "worked": "$$\\frac15+\\frac1{25}+\\frac1{125}+\\cdots$$\n$a=\\frac15$, $r=\\frac15$. Since $|r|<1$, the limiting sum exists.\n$$\\begin{align*}S_\\infty&=\\frac{a}{1-r}\\\\S_\\infty&=\\frac{\\frac15}{1-\\frac15}\\\\S_\\infty&=\\frac14\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}7\\left(\\frac12\\right)^n$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac72+\\frac74+\\frac78+\\cdots$; $a=\\frac72$, $r=\\frac12$; $S_\\infty=7$.",
          "worked": "$$\\frac72+\\frac74+\\frac78+\\cdots$$\n$a=\\frac72$, $r=\\frac12$. Since $|r|<1$, the limiting sum exists.\n$$\\begin{align*}S_\\infty&=\\frac{a}{1-r}\\\\S_\\infty&=\\frac{\\frac72}{1-\\frac12}\\\\S_\\infty&=7\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}40\\left(-\\frac35\\right)^n$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-24+\\frac{72}{5}-\\frac{216}{25}+\\cdots$; $a=-24$, $r=-\\frac35$; $S_\\infty=-15$.",
          "worked": "$$-24+\\frac{72}{5}-\\frac{216}{25}+\\cdots$$\n$a=-24$, $r=-\\frac35$. Since $|r|<1$, the limiting sum exists.\n$$\\begin{align*}S_\\infty&=\\frac{a}{1-r}\\\\S_\\infty&=\\frac{-24}{1-\\left(-\\frac35\\right)}\\\\S_\\infty&=\\frac{-24}{\\frac85}\\\\S_\\infty&=-15\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 37
